  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nAn upper-level ridge of high pressure is centered over the Tennessee \nValley today. Waves of mid-level vorticity continue to track around \nthe northern periphery of the ridge, mainly across Michigan, \nsoutheast Ohio, and Pennsylvania. This is where most \nthunderstorm complexes will be focused today, but a few high \nresolution model solutions show the southern edge of these \ncomplexes reaching parts of northern West Virginia and southeast\nOhio late this evening and into tonight. The Storm Prediction \nCenter has placed these areas in a Slight Risk of severe weather\ntoday, with the main risks being damaging wind gusts and hail.\n\nThe upper-level ridge axis is expected to migrate westward Friday, \nwhich could allow for a few mid-level shortwaves to track across \nsoutheast Ohio and northern West Virginia Friday afternoon and again \nSaturday afternoon. Coverage of showers and thunderstorms will be \nmore scattered across the forecast area Friday and Saturday compared \nto today because of the shifting ridge axis and an advancing cold \nfront. Again, the main risks of any severe thunderstorms will be \ndamaging wind gusts and hail.\n\nA thunderstorm or two cannot be ruled out Sunday in the mountains, \nbut Sunday should overall be drier in the wake of the cold front as \ndrier air filters back into the region from the north.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nExcessive heat and humidity will continue today and Friday, \nespecially across the lowlands, with high temperatures in the middle \nto upper 90s and heat index values in the lower 100s. Heat \nAdvisories will remain in effect until Friday evening. As a cold \nfront approaches Saturday, widespread clouds will keep temperatures \nbelow heat advisory criteria. Some relief from the heat will arrive \nin the wake of the cold front Sunday with high temperatures in the \nmiddle and upper 80s. Dew points will drop to the upper 60s and \nlower 70s by Sunday. The air won't feel excessively humid like the \npast several days, but it will still feel somewhat muggy.",
